iciembre supone el 5 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 48 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.399,15 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: Ajustar a la baja el importe no implica irregularidad. Puede ser por normas, presupuestos o necesidades específicas. No refleja actos maliciosos ni omisiones.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] cubren la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros sectores. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se ajustan a un patrón regular.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 82 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 22.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.7 to 4.8. December accounts for 10% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 12. Contract [1], for 14,399.15 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. Statistical patterns can reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing. The data alone does not indicate fraud or errors in the procurement process.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for consistency with other contracts in the same period. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service or product. Verify if the December contracts were part of a larger procurement plan or separate initiatives.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["Z%2F0Xs4X%2BgcxQFSeKCRun4Q%3D%3D","C3ajx